tion\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/Successors","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The closure’s row for one vertex, each target checked to be a vertex as it is read (not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when the row is formed). A struct rather than a lazy map, so an algorithm that keeps an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"iterator per vertex on its stack (Tarjan’s) allocates nothing for it.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph.Successors","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Successors"}]}}}